 "why": "Done, but odd-looking: Intro to Blender lesson 2 (\"the sphere is half size\"). The learner pressed S 0.5 and then, out of habit from another tutorial, Ctrl+A > Apply > Scale. Applying bakes the scale into the mesh, so the object's scale reads [1, 1, 1] again while its dimensions are 1 x 1 x 1 m, half of the default 2 m UV sphere. The sphere is half size; only the scale field stopped saying so.",
